  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Nifurpirinol and HEp-2 through a series of target-mediated pathways. Nifurpirinol is implicated in targeting UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which is a target of Aeruginosin DA722 and 3,3',5-Trihydroxybibenzyl. Both of these compounds have been shown to interact with HEp-2, the human epithelial cell line, indicating a possible downstream effect on the cell. Similarly, Nifurpirinol is also associated with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which is targeted by Euphoscopin A, which also affects HEp-2. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with varying degrees of support from different targets. The evidence highlights the role of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase enzymes in mediating the interaction between Nifurpirinol and HEp-2, suggesting that these enzymes may be key intermediaries in the biological response. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the importance of further experimental validation to confirm the direct effect of Nifurpirinol on HEp-2."
